cation/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"cc3297671ca0cdd0c0d4eee590cd23f0484b84309cc880fb8b2e770987e9bf4b","event_uuid":"6c95d137-13e1-4a20-afc4-09a72c0a7f19","position":{"commit_sha":"82001e6f1f2efd42960e852b7827f92cdeff55bb","position":"1795420295587678001-6c95d137-13e1-4a20-afc4-09a72c0a7f19"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced 2026-11-22 21:30-21:55 PST on main c924c0ea2e8 with a stalling PATH git shim (init bound shortened to 3 s): fresh init paid 5 bounds plus unbounded remote get-url probes (195 s); an already-initialized store whose rev-parse timed out was pruned and its tracker directory deleted (8 bounds, 204 s); an init stopped after worktree add --orphan reported success and the next init never made the initial commit, never committed .pre-commit-config.yaml and never set commit.gpgsign. Plan written into the description; acceptance criteria unchanged.","timestamp":1795413256669283001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented in commit on worktree bug-75fe-init-timeout (from gerrit main c924c0ea2e8). Plan-review advisories adopted: the resume runs under the init lock and re-checks the marker; a failed root commit keeps the marker and returns 1; raw-git-ok sanctions on the new helpers; pending_init_attaches_to_existing also probes through the bounded seam (pending_init_remote_unreachable keeps run_git because it shares run_git_fn with the network probe). New tests (9): 8 fail on main, all pass on the fix. Real stalling-shim rerun with a 3 s bound: fresh init 3.0 s / 1 bound (was 195 s / 5 bounds + unbounded probes), mounted store 3.0 s / 1 bound with the tracker intact (was 204 s / 8 bounds and the tracker deleted). make verify running.","timestamp":1795414981368831001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 3531 merged as 27df71b298b (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved, submitted 23:37 PST). make verify on 27df71b298b before push: exit 0 (21849 passed / 34 skipped default tier, 231 passed / 2 skipped integration). AC evidence: (1) init._git raises GitTimedOut; tests test_a_timed_out_probe_never_deletes_a_mounted_tracker, test_auto_init_reports_a_timeout_instead_of_creating_a_store, test_a_timed_out_rebase_continue_is_not_followed_by_abort. (2) test_a_fully_stalled_fresh_init_stops_after_one_bound and the real stalling-shim rerun: 1 bound, 3.0 s, for fresh and mounted stores. (3) test_an_init_stopped_mid_bootstrap_is_finished_by_the_next_init and test_a_failed_root_commit_keeps_the_bootstrap_pending. Closing.","timestamp":1795419829808987001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795404802912952001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0c93e470-7ead-4f75-8142-6e61ebfda168","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7bef-6755-be56-4a43"},{"link_uuid":"825a0a41-06eb-43f4-b4cd-c4e68ed518a9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b53e-2623-c234-48f8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFound while fixing hilarious-loony-crayfish (2026-11-22). `rebar init`'s own bootstrap git calls go through `init._git` (`run_git_write`, check=False), and callers read a watchdog timeout (exit 124, empty stdout) as an answer. Example: `_ensure_branch_user_config` treats a timed-out `config user.email` as unset and issues 4 more config calls; the `commit.gpgsign`/`tag.gpgsign` writes in `_mount_or_create_branch` discard their results. On a stalled filesystem each sequential call pays its own 120 s bound. Reproduced with a git shim that stalls tracker `git config`: the store fixture of tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py hit its 300 s pytest-timeout inside `_ensure_branch_user_config`.\n\nSimply raising from `init._git` is not safe: it also serves the auto-init predicates (`pending_init_is_symlink`, `pending_init_attaches_to_existing`, `pending_init_remote_unreachable`) called from `_cli/_init.py` without a handler, and init's rebase recovery catches `Exception`. Stopping after `worktree add --orphan` but before the initial commit leaves a tracker that the next `rebar init` treats as already initialized, so the bootstrap steps never re-run.\n\n## Reproduction (2026-11-22, main at c924c0ea2e8)\nA PATH git shim that hangs every call once a flag file exists, with init's `run_git_write` bound shortened to 3 s (scratch script, not committed):\n- Fresh init, everything stalled: 5 calls each paid the bound (`config --get`, `rev-parse --verify` x2, `worktree add` x2); the 2 timed-out `rev-parse --verify` were read as \"no ticket branch\". The `git remote get-url` probes (`_init_probe.remote_exists`, `require_s3_helper_if_s3_remote`, src/rebar/_commands/_init_probe.py:77-99) run through `run_git` with no timeout at all, so they hung until the shim gave up (about 60 s each). Total 195 s.\n- Already-initialized store, then stalled: the timed-out `rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree` was read as \"not a worktree\", so init ran `worktree prune` and `_rmtree(tracker)` (init.py:186-188): the mounted tracker directory was deleted. 8 bounds, 204 s.\n- Stop after `worktree add --orphan` (stubbed seam): the first init still printed \"initialized\" with rc 0 after 17 timed-out calls. The next `rebar init` said \"already initialized\": no `chore: initialize ticket tracker` commit, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` left untracked, `commit.gpgsign` never set; the ensure sweep's commits became the branch root.\n\n## Approach\n1. `init._git` (src/rebar/_commands/init.py:56) raises `GitTimedOut` through `raise_if_watchdog_timeout`, exactly like the ensure units' seam (`_init_ensures._git`, src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py:57; `GitTimedOut` in src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py:281-295). `_git_ok` inherits it, so no timed-out call is read as false, unset, or success.\n2. `init_core` catches `GitTimedOut` once, at the top: it writes `Error: git <op> timed out during rebar init; nothing after it ran. Re-run 'rebar init' to finish.` and returns 1. The init lock is still released by the existing `finally`. The first timeout therefore ends init: one bound.\n3. `_pin_auto_maintenance` stops swallowing `GitTimedOut` (it currently logs and continues into further stalled calls); the timeout propagates to step 2. Init's rebase recovery re-raises `GitTimedOut` ahead of its `except Exception`, so a timed-out `rebase --continue` is not followed by `rebase --abort`.\n4. The local `git remote get-url` probes init makes go through a bounded seam: init passes a `run_git_fn` adapter over `_git` to `_init_probe.remote_exists` and `require_s3_helper_if_s3_remote`. The network probe (`probe_remote_branch`, `run_bounded_git`) keeps its own `REMOTE_PROBE_TIMEOUT`.\n5. Auto-init (src/rebar/_cli/_init.py:43-79): the `pending_init_*` predicates now propagate `GitTimedOut`; `_create_tracker` catches it, reports it, and exits 1 without prompting or creating a store, so a timeout can never be read as \"no store exists\". The best-effort path at _cli/_init.py:176-180 already catches `Exception`.\n6. Resumable bootstrap: init writes a `ticket-init.pending` file beside the existing `ticket-init.lock` (the common git dir, `_init_lock_dir`) before `_mount_or_create_branch`, and removes it only after the bootstrap completes. The orphan arm's tail (user config, `commit.gpgsign`/`tag.gpgsign` false, the initial empty commit) moves into a `_finish_bootstrap(repo, tracker)` helper that also runs the existing `_ensure_branch_user_config`, `_exclude_scratch_in_tracker`, `_commit_precommit`, `_gen_local_files`; it makes the initial commit only while the tracker's HEAD is unborn. On the already-mounted path, when the pending file exists, init runs `_finish_bootstrap`, removes the file, then runs the ensure sweep as today. Without the file, re-init behaves as today. All steps are already idempotent or guarded.\n\nNo config key, `REBAR_*` env var or flag is added; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` must exit 0.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py — steps 1-4 and 6.\n- src/rebar/_cli/_init.py — step 5.\n- tests/unit/test_init_bootstrap_timeout.py (new) — tests below.\n- tests/unit/test_ensure_git_timeout.py — the pin test now expects the timeout to propagate.\n\n## Testing\nUnit tests stub `run_git_write` to return the watchdog's own result (code 124), as tests/unit/test_ensure_git_timeout.py does, so nothing sleeps:\n- Fresh init with every git call stalled: `init_core` returns 1 after exactly 1 git call; stderr names the operation and tells the user to re-run; no tracker directory exists.\n- Already-initialized store with `rev-parse` stalled: returns 1 after 1 call; the tracker directory still exists (no prune, no rmtree).\n- Stall after `worktree add --orphan`: returns 1 after 1 stalled call; the pending file exists. A second `init_core` with real git: rc 0, the branch root commit is `chore: initialize ticket tracker`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` is committed, `commit.gpgsign` is `false`, the pending file is gone. A third init makes no bootstrap commit.\n- Auto-init: `_create_tracker` with a stalled `rev-parse` raises `SystemExit(1)` and never calls `init_core`.\n- Rebase recovery: a timed-out `rebase --continue` returns 1 with no `rebase --abort` call.\n- Pin: `_pin_auto_maintenance` propagates `GitTimedOut` after 1 call.\n- Re-run the scratch shim reproduction against the fix: fresh and mounted runs each pay 1 bound and the mounted tracker survives.\n- `make verify` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A timed-out git in init's bootstrap is not treated as success or as an unset value.\n- [x] A stalled filesystem costs `rebar init` at most one git bound before it reports the failure.\n- [x] An init stopped mid-bootstrap is completed by the next `rebar init`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"raise on git watchdog timeout, stop init at first timeout, bounded remote probes, resumable bootstrap"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_init.py","reason":"auto-init reports a git timeout instead of treating it as no store"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_init_bootstrap_timeout.py","reason":"new tests for timeout handling and resume"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ensure_git_timeout.py","reason":"pin test expects the timeout to propagate"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b53e-2623-c234-48f8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6a28356f-e104-469b-822c-218ba21ce011","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"75fe-db94-fcee-44da","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar init bootstrap reads a timed-out git as an answer and pays one 120 s bound per call","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["67e1e11e-c5ff-4b55-99d5-9a9447a805be","d8b496eb-66d9-4aea-8e77-3a21787b9a13","4aeab966-aca2-4e97-8a11-709592ffcef6","d8a718d4-de71-4534-9fd7-8568f7e67951","ffd015c3-1e37-499b-b188-b930f4917a01","dadc5ee1-8f83-4cb0-9d8b-54f6e4f98db6","54e3ad2b-a581-4d88-80cb-05d720bf717b","825a0a41-06eb-43f4-b4cd-c4e68ed518a9","0c6edfd6-c811-4aff-aacc-22eff22f7f63","91c3de45-1c7b-4637-854e-7f8251b3cbd0","6a28356f-e104-469b-822c-218ba21ce011","6c95d137-13e1-4a20-afc4-09a72c0a7f19"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795420295587678002,"uuid":"bd3ac9fd-47b3-4b74-b611-fabe0810d01e"}